1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sunset
floating on the Nakagawa

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
When I kick a pebble, even my shoe flies off

3
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:32,920
Onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,160
They laughed that I was still just a brat

5
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
Pachinko, one yawn, nothing changes

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,180
The streets feel strangely kind

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointed hat's water bottle

9
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:07,460
Natural interpretation, and the sun sinks

10
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness lost again

12
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,500
Because I've realized I'm a fool

13
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:31,680
Lightning Marriage: Kankichi Ryotsu

14
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:50,520
You bastard!

15
00:01:58,580 --> 00:01:59,480
Lord Ryo

16
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,720
Maria! Catch that guy!

17
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,580
But Kenpon is...

18
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,260
Permission granted!

19
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,300
Yes, Lord Ryo!

20
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,400
Get out of the way, you horse!

21
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,900
Well done, Maria!

22
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,980
I'm so glad I could be of service.

23
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,820
Lord Ryo, who is this man?

24
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,780
He's a wedding gift money thief!

25
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:25,140
I was attending a childhood
friend's wedding in Asakusa,

26
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,160
when I ran into him.

27
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,900
So that's why you're wearing a suit,
Lord Ryo.

28
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,580
You look wonderful.

29
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,900
This thing's too tight, I can't take it.

30
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:35,840
What's with you? Wearing a kimono and all?

31
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,060
I'm on my way back from a tea ceremony.

32
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:39,220
It suits you pretty well, you know.

33
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:40,980
Ryo-sama, how delightful!

34
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:42,520
Stop it, in front of people!

35
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:46,040
After that arrest, your lovely kimono is -

36
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,580
I can't go home like this,
I'm so embarrassed.

37
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:51,100
Can't you dress yourself?

38
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:52,560
Yes.

39
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,320
What should we do?

40
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,440
My family home is just nearby.

41
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,360
Let's have Mom fix it.

42
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:02,940
I get to meet Ryo-san's mother?

43
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,380
I'm so moved.

44
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,280
On second thought, let's not.

45
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:06,800
Come on.

46
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,340
Please let me greet your parents.

47
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:10,700
What are you talking about?

48
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:13,020
We're just going there
to get your obi fixed!

49
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,240
So you really are going to say it?

50
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:19,060
Don't say it.

51
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:25,740
The family home was a tsukudani shop,
you see.

52
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,840
Hey! Is anyone home?

53
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:34,300
That's odd, the shop's open though.

54
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,160
Money just lying around here...

55
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,000
They've forgotten to put
away a huge sum of cash.

56
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,800
What are they thinking,
running a business like this?

57
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,520
It's a messy place, but just come on in.

58
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:44,920
Yes.

59
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,740
Hey, Dad! Mom!

60
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:50,920
Leaving the pot on the stove like this,
honestly.

61
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,060
Young Master Ryo, a guest is here.

62
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,220
Isn't that Kan-chan?

63
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:57,280
Auntie, long time no see.

64
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:58,960
Oh no!

65
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,280
I'm counting on you over there.

66
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:02,960
Yes.

67
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,540
Did you quit your job and
decide to take over the shop?

68
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,380
No way, it's just for today.

69
00:04:09,380 --> 00:04:11,380
Is this about right for 200 grams?

70
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:12,920
But here's a little extra.

71
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,780
Nice service. How much is it?

72
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,880
What? There's no price written anywhere!

73
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:20,540
What the hell, 100 yen is fine.

74
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:22,040
Are you sure?

75
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:23,340
Yeah, today's on the house.

76
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:25,840
It's a shop run as a hobby anyway.

77
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,680
Even if it goes under, it's no big deal.

78
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,140
Then, 100 yen and...

79
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:29,640
Thanks for your business.

80
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:34,080
Mom, that lady in the kimono earlier,
is she going to be your bride?

81
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,260
No, no, not at all.

82
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,160
Playing dumb again

83
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,560
Hello long time no see.

84
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,740
Aren't you Gin-san's son?

85
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:44,200
You're still alive

86
00:04:46,080 --> 00:04:48,900
Officer,
did you get fired and come back to the shop?

87
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:50,220
No, it's just that today...

88
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:52,320
Wan-chan, I hear you're getting married!

89
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,040
What, really?

90
00:04:54,460 --> 00:04:56,280
No, no, today it just happened that...

91
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:59,280
Well, good for you.
I thought you'd never be able to marry.

92
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,900
I told you, that's not it!

93
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:03,960
I'm done over here, I'll help you.

94
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,440
Oh my, she's a real beauty, isn't she?

95
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:09,500
How did you trick her?
You rascal, you rascal!

96
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:10,540
So that's why...

97
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,100
You two are already so lovey-dovey,
aren't you?

98
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:14,100
Really, really!

99
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,360
What can I get for you?

100
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,360
300 grams of clam tsukudani, please.

101
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,020
Yes.

102
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,020
Thank you for waiting.

103
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,420
Ryo-san, how much is this?

104
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:28,620
Today everything's just 100 yen.

105
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,380
Okay, then it's 100 yen.

106
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:33,600
Nice service.
It's a world of difference from Gin-san.

107
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,440
Really, really.

108
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,720
If it's that cheap,
I think I'll take this and this.

109
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:40,820
By the way, Kan-chan,
when Gin-san gets back,

110
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:45,280
tell him the Keiro-kai trip
has been set for June 29th.

111
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,720
The 29th of September, got it.

112
00:05:47,900 --> 00:05:49,400
Well then, be happy.

113
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,440
If you don't even get a single yen,
you're really useless.

114
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,320
Gin-san, Gin-san!

115
00:05:59,440 --> 00:05:59,940
Yo.

116
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:02,980
Good thing your son
found himself a nice bride.

117
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:03,460
See you.

118
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,260
What's that dad going on about?

119
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:11,220
What is it?

120
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:23,860
What can I get for you?

121
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,600
I think I'll take some
of the Inaho tsukudani.

122
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:28,420
Here you go.

123
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:32,100
Are you free tonight?

124
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:37,580
If you're free, how about coming with me
to the night races at Kawasaki Racecourse?

125
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,480
Dad.

126
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:40,400
Kankichi.

127
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,140
Why are you shopping at your own store?

128
00:06:43,140 --> 00:06:43,620
Ugh.

129
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,760
Dad, you haven't met her yet, right?

130
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,080
Everyone calls her Maria.

131
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,400
Nice to meet you, Father.

132
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:52,280
The pleasure is mine.

133
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:53,940
Tomode Kankichi.

134
00:06:53,940 --> 00:06:55,060
Where's Mom?

135
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:56,500
I came over here, so...

136
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:58,080
The shop was empty, you know.

137
00:06:58,620 --> 00:07:00,120
I'm running late.

138
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,220
I'm home.

139
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,280
Kankichi.

140
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:11,140
Kankichi.

141
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:13,460
You're back safe and sound.

142
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:16,000
Mama's so happy, Mama's so happy.

143
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:18,000
Cut it out, in front of people.

144
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,480
Where did you run off to,
leaving the shop like that?

145
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:23,560
Just went out shopping.

146
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:27,380
Once things calm down here,
help Maria put on her kimono, okay?

147
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:28,860
Yeah, yeah, I know.

148
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:30,520
Thanks for your business!

149
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:34,520
Dad, Dad, who's that cute girl?

150
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:38,520
Apparently she's a coworker, but the
rumor is she's Kankichi's girlfriend.

151
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:41,700
I mean, she came calling in a kimono, so...

152
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,940
Hey, maybe this is it!

153
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:48,940
Mom, are you done yet?

154
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,660
Almost done.

155
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:55,500
There, that should do it.

156
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,500
Thank you very much.

157
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:58,880
Anyway, I'm going to ask you straight out,

158
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:01,140
do you like Kankichi, Maria?

159
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,780
Yes, of course I do.

160
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:06,840
It's not a dream.

161
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,840
Hey, Dad, come here for a second.

162
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:11,200
Why?

163
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:12,880
Dad, listen.

164
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:13,620
What?

165
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,140
Really, Mom?

166
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,637
If she likes the other person,

167
00:08:18,687 --> 00:08:21,340
then it's basically 100% settled, isn't it!

168
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:24,920
He must have made up his
mind to take over this shop.

169
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:26,484
As expected of the eldest son.

170
00:08:26,534 --> 00:08:29,580
So he has been thinking ahead.

171
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:33,140
Maria, please look after Kankichi.

172
00:08:33,340 --> 00:08:34,100
Nice to meet you.

173
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:36,660
N-no, likewise, nice to meet you.

174
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,200
Please take care of him for years to come.

175
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:43,200
Why are you being so formal?

176
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,940
Maria, if you're done, let's go.

177
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,740
I'll show you around Sensō-ji, then.

178
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,280
That's right, one-on-one, one-on-one.

179
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:51,560
Yes.

180
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:52,820
See you.

181
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:54,040
Thank you for everything.

182
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,580
Come again, won't you?

183
00:08:55,580 --> 00:08:55,940
Yes.

184
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,580
I forgot.

185
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,560
Kankichi, have you set a date?

186
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:04,420
It's been set for June 29th, so

187
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:07,140
June 29th

188
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:07,880
I see.

189
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,020
You've got a tough time ahead.

190
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,640
So you went and decided it

191
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,840
Mom, let's send them off with a banzai!

192
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,440
Walky-walky.

193
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:19,300
Bye-bye-bye-bye!

194
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:22,740
Stop it, how embarrassing.
Come on, Maria, let's go.

195
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:23,260
Yes.

196
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:27,000
Bye-bye-bye-bye-bye!

197
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,700
You're in luck, aren't you?

198
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,100
What are you getting so excited about?

199
00:09:35,150 --> 00:09:50,940
That idiooooooooot...

200
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:51,180
I know.

201
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:55,220
Anyway, nothing but good things
like this could ever happen.

202
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,060
So that means I can make rice balls too

203
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,680
So that means I can do this too.

204
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,480
Yes, Father.

205
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:09,380
Father, how does it taste?

206
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,140
It's delicious.

207
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,220
And this too.

208
00:10:15,240 --> 00:10:16,780
How is it, Father?

209
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:18,920
It's really good.

210
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:19,040
Nyaaan.

211
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,760
Now the front too, please!

212
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:22,620
Nyaa.

213
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:26,100
And then I started helping
with the tsukudani too.

214
00:10:28,540 --> 00:10:31,220
Father, could you do a taste test for me?

215
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,040
Wait!

216
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:43,800
Aaaaah!

217
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:48,600
We're nowhere near the 300-year
taste of the Ryotsu family.

218
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:49,980
Still not good enough.

219
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:51,100
I'm terribly sorry.

220
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:51,960
Father.

221
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,320
I'm Nakura Maria.

222
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,800
The path of tsukudani is long and hard.

223
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,380
Let's walk it step by step, together.

224
00:10:59,380 --> 00:11:01,380
Father.

225
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:04,140
There, there, there, there.

226
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:10,140
Now I'm in a bind

227
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:12,300
Having a daughter changes your whole life.

228
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:13,620
Well, that's a problem.

229
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:21,820
Ugh, look at him grinning to himself.
It's creepy.

230
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:27,080
But that girl would make a lovely shop girl,
wouldn't she?

231
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:29,860
That'd bring in customers by the dozen.

232
00:11:29,860 --> 00:11:30,380
Hello.

233
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,160
I hear your son's wedding has been set.

234
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:35,980
A congratulatory gift from
the neighborhood association.

235
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:37,520
You shouldn't have.

236
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,760
Gin-san can finally rest easy now.

237
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:43,320
A weight's finally off our shoulders,
isn't it, Mother?

238
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:44,820
Coming, Father.

239
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:48,700
Why would that good-for-nothing
decide to settle down?

240
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:52,480
I've been waiting so long for this day.

241
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,300
I understand, Yone-chan.

242
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,080
Mom.

243
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:58,400
Kankichi's actually getting married?!

244
00:11:59,540 --> 00:12:01,580
But when I look back,
ever since I was five years old,

245
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:04,720
it's been decades since they
tore down the old building.

246
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:07,060
Finally, even that
good-for-nothing is getting married.

247
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,360
So, we'd like to kindly
ask for your cooperation.

248
00:12:09,920 --> 00:12:12,640
How exciting!
Let's make that day a grand one somehow.

249
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:13,540
Thank you very much.

250
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:18,080
For the reception, let's offer up that hall.

251
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,380
What?

252
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,460
W-wow, that's amazing!

253
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:26,020
Gin-san! Gin-san!

254
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:29,300
What's going on?

255
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:31,100
Something huge has happened!

256
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:35,680
The shopping district has decided to hold a
parade through the whole town for the wedding!

257
00:12:36,300 --> 00:13:03,680
!

258
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,680
Looks like you're quite the wild one

259
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,180
Hey, Ryo-san!

260
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,940
Why didn't you tell us
you were getting married?

261
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,340
Senpai is getting married?

262
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:20,380
That's got to be a lie.

263
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:22,080
Yesterday, your father

264
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:23,800
called me,
the first time since your greeting visit.

265
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,500
Wait just a minute, please!

266
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,400
Who are you marrying? Who?

267
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,960
I didn't ask for the details, but

268
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,760
last week a beautiful woman in a kimono

269
00:13:30,760 --> 00:13:32,960
came with you to greet us, he said.

270
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:38,240
Nothing like that!
Could it be... could it be...?

271
00:13:38,800 --> 00:13:48,020
Well, the other day I went to my parents' place with Maria.
So that's why your attitude has seemed off since you introduced Maria on Ahan Street.

272
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:56,140
What, you're happy about it, Chief? Didn't I say she's a man?
Now that you mention it, I forgot to tell you.

273
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,160
They probably mistook you for his fiancée.

274
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:01,640
So are we really getting married?

275
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:03,120
I'm so happy.

276
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:07,360
Hey, wait! It's not that simple.
We're both men, after all.

277
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:10,180
That's right, if you miss this day,
you'll never get married in your life!

278
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:10,980
Just leave me alone.

279
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,920
But if the Chief has been contacted too,
that means

280
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:18,200
This is bad.
Maria, come with me for a moment.

281
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:18,680
Yes!

282
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,820
Chief, I'm borrowing the patrol car!

283
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:25,340
To Asakusa! Go to Asakusa!

284
00:14:26,140 --> 00:14:27,920
This isn't a taxi, you know.

285
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:29,420
When I say go, you go!

286
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:30,520
Y-yes!

287
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:46,020
Kankichi's great-grandfather and
my father were the best of friends.

288
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:50,160
Even from the afterlife, he asked me
to make Kankichi's wedding a grand one.

289
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:52,300
He was a hateful little brat, though,

290
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:58,940
so I'll step up as host and make it a grand affair.
Two hundred guests from all over the country will be gathering, you see.

291
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:09,200
Nagauta, city councillors, Japanese dance, kōdan, rakugo...
Just the greetings from both families alone, that's 28 people?

292
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:13,600
The ceremony will take five hours after all, won't it?
Kankichi is the eldest son.

293
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:15,060
Shouldn't we make it a grand affair, then?

294
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:17,200
But five hours is a bit much.

295
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:20,160
Why not just take a
ten-minute break in between?

296
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:21,720
Like those epic films, you know,

297
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:23,400
That's a great idea.

298
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,820
The budget will also run quite high, though.

299
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,380
How much will it come to in total?

300
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:30,380
It's already over 10 million yen.

301
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:30,920
What?

302
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:33,200
Did we really have that much in savings?

303
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,640
Of course we don't.

304
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:35,440
Right.

305
00:15:35,440 --> 00:15:37,780
We never even thought
about getting him married.

306
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:39,040
Don't worry.

307
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:41,780
The last place could easily
fit about 1,000 people, right?

308
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:45,560
Let's say it's 30,000 yen per person, right?

309
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:47,980
With 1,000 guests,
that's 30 million yen in income.

310
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:51,180
We get the ceremony for free and
still make 20 million yen in profit.

311
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:53,400
I see, that's our grandpa for you.

312
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:56,100
The more people we invite,
the more budget we have left over.

313
00:15:57,100 --> 00:16:00,020
Since we have the budget, let's make
the ceremony even more extravagant.

314
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:03,440
How about a parade through
Asakusa in an open-top car?

315
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:07,780
That's a great idea!
Let's bring in the animals too.

316
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:08,940
This is going to be a blast.

317
00:16:09,620 --> 00:16:12,000
How about calling it a boat
parade on the Sumida River?

318
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:18,520
Come on, with 500 business owners invited, they'll
be holding a party wedding all night long, right?

319
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:24,260
A 24-hour wedding! That's settled, then...

320
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:25,980
What is this?

321
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:36,240
They've already turned it into a business, making everything a festival.
Geez, they even made signboards, dammit!

322
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:43,120
Ryo-san, congratulations!

323
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,200
So you're the bride
everyone's been talking about?

324
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:47,960
She's a total beauty!
You lucky bastard, you lucky bastard!

325
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:48,880
Shut up!

326
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,640
W-what's the matter with you?

327
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,680
Do you know where Dad and Mom are?

328
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:56,800
I think they're at the Gachon Hall in Gachon Temple,
I believe.

329
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,500
You'll cry too!

330
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,860
Hey! That useless man's head, you know!

331
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:09,960
Hey, you!

332
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,580
Perfect, put this on for me.

333
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:14,540
Throw this in too.

334
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:20,980
And the size fits perfectly.

335
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:23,540
Isn't this fine for the
groom's entrance style?

336
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:26,260
After all, it's a five-hour wedding.

337
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:29,240
You need to mix things up,
or people will get bored.

338
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,880
Dad, I need to talk to you.

339
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:33,820
What is it?

340
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,640
Maria was here too?

341
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:39,840
Kankichi,
we have to introduce her to everyone.

342
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,640
When did I ever say I'd get married?

343
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:44,200
Don't play dumb, you bastard.

344
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,600
What are you talking about now?

345
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,560
You said the date was set for June 29th,
didn't you?

346
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,880
June 29th.

347
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:53,360
That's the date for the Keiroukai trip.

348
00:17:54,300 --> 00:17:56,040
You jumped to conclusions on your own,
you idiot.

349
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:59,320
But you are going to marry her, right?

350
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,800
As if I could!

351
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,620
This Maria is a man!

352
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:04,580
Heh heh heh.

353
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:06,120
Quit kidding around, you.

354
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:07,980
Don't talk nonsense, you idiot.

355
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:10,040
Then go check for yourself.

356
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:59,800
!

357
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:01,980
Crying won't change anything now.
The venue's already booked, you know.

358
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:04,280
You're the one who went ahead and
decided everything on your own, Dad!

359
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:07,340
We can't exactly say it was a mistake now.
What are you going to do?

360
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,080
I don't know anything about that.

361
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,480
Even if it's a guy, I won't discriminate.
Just get married.

362
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:12,540
Don't be ridiculous.

363
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:15,580
You want me to give up the
30 million yen in gift money?

364
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:16,160
What?

365
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,260
Damn.

366
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:22,140
See, Dad? You were trying to make money off my wedding,
weren't you?

367
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:24,240
Mom, you're getting
married just to harass us.

368
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:27,540
What are you doing?
We're still in the middle of planning!

369
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:30,460
It's nothing, I'll be right there.

370
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,480
Yeah, yeah.

371
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:32,980
Is that so?

372
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:39,240
So how much will the profit
be after deducting expenses?

373
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,480
No way.

374
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:43,580
Either way, we can't back out now, right?

375
00:19:44,240 --> 00:19:46,160
It's gotten this exciting already.

376
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:48,940
Can't be helped.
Let's just go ahead with it now.

377
00:19:48,940 --> 00:19:50,280
At least let's take the gift money.

378
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,960
We'll split the profits evenly, right?

379
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:54,780
But if we get caught, it'll be a disaster.

380
00:19:55,380 --> 00:19:58,340
Don't worry. I've got a good idea.

381
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,500
Yes, this is Director Mizusawa.

382
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:05,620
It's the visitor from the other day.

383
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:07,500
A super-special plan!

384
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,640
Asakusa's Samba Carnival
and the Sanja Festival,

385
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:13,220
plus the Sumida River fireworks,
all viewable together.

386
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,880
Ratings of 50% are guaranteed!

387
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:18,860
Is that really true? Tell me more.

388
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:26,040
Ladies and gentlemen, guests,
this is Kankichi Ryotsu!

389
00:20:26,040 --> 00:20:28,500
We are now heading to the venue.

390
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:39,420
Thanks to all of you,
I was able to get married like this.

391
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:41,540
I hope this is really going to be okay.

392
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,340
Don't worry, I've got it covered.

393
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:48,220
Ladies and gentlemen,
we apologize for the constant disturbance.

394
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,500
Just like Kan-chan

395
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,580
The Sanja Festival, the Samba Carnival,

396
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:55,560
and they've even dragged
in a fireworks show.

397
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:58,660
Look, even the TV station
is broadcasting it live.

398
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:02,980
Yes, right there,
zoom in on that the whole time.

399
00:21:02,980 --> 00:21:04,320
Get some good shots, Ana-chan.

400
00:21:04,320 --> 00:21:07,400
The car passes through the shopping
street and enters Gachon Dera.

401
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:09,800
Here in the Gachon Dera hall,

402
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:11,580
it can accommodate 1,000 people.

403
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:13,460
Quicker than the four seasons,
the banquet comes first.

404
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:14,780
We're starting from Kōen.

405
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,800
Is it really okay for
him to make it this grand?

406
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,280
I wonder how they plan to cover it up.

407
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:35,760
What on earth is going on?

408
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,320
Nobody from the groom's side has come,
can you believe it?

409
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,720
Thank you all for your long wait.

410
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:42,840
Here come the bride and groom.

411
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,160
Please welcome them with
a big round of applause.

412
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:50,440
Looks like the kimono got dirty after all

413
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:54,020
Since it's a man anyway,
I've decided to just go along with it.

414
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:00,480
Dad, that's great.

415
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:03,360
I'm happy for you.

416
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:06,140
Kankichi, you can't run away now!

417
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,480
Sorry, everyone.

418
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:15,340
It was all a prank camera!

419
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:20,140
What a surprise!
Well, I was completely fooled too!

420
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:20,980
Hahaha!

421
00:22:21,560 --> 00:22:23,980
Everyone's so good at fooling people, Maria!

422
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:26,800
As if I'd ever get married!

423
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:29,560
Got tricked so easily!

424
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:30,040
Gah!

425
00:22:30,560 --> 00:22:31,620
Phew!

426
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:34,260
So it was all a surprise after all.

427
00:22:34,780 --> 00:22:35,540
Hehehe.

428
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:41,680
That it was all a lie!

429
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:43,040
No way...

430
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:45,480
What is that idiot thinking?

431
00:22:45,480 --> 00:22:47,380
He'll never go for this.

432
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:48,660
Overjoyed...

433
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:51,660
It was a great chance for all the relatives to get together,
wasn't it?

434
00:22:52,380 --> 00:22:54,300
Don't deceive the whole shopping district!

435
00:22:55,580 --> 00:22:57,920
You lot cashed in on it too,
profiting off this!

436
00:22:57,920 --> 00:22:59,880
Hand over the gift money, you bastard!

437
00:23:00,520 --> 00:23:04,960
You bastard, you tricked us!

438
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:18,620
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee...

439
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,400
You tricked us, Kankichi!

440
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,420
Did you make a profit?

441
00:23:23,460 --> 00:23:24,200
Your address?

442
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:26,340
He's passed out.

443
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:27,380
Your address?

444
00:23:27,380 --> 00:23:28,340
Your address?

445
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:33,640
Aaaaaaah!

446
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:34,840
Aaaaaaah!

447
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:47,700
We caught that thief the other day, but leaving it to him was a mistake.
I didn't know, I swear.

448
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:51,000
What an undutiful child you are.

449
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,600
Let's head home, let's head home.

450
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,040
I win.

451
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,920
No way,
I'm absolutely not giving this one back.

452
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:08,540
Is a rookie trainee officer
really coming to this police box?

453
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:09,740
Leave it to me.

454
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:13,700
This Senior Patrol Officer Kankichi Ryotsu is
someone you won't be embarrassed to send anywhere.

455
00:24:13,700 --> 00:24:16,760
I'll whip him into a proper police officer.

456
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:21,480
Ryo-san,
good luck with the new recruit's training.

457
00:24:48,700 --> 00:24:59,160
I want to ride a cycle,
I want to be freer than a bird.

458
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:07,080
At the speed of a kaleidoscope,
the lady's dream keeps changing.

459
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:15,280
Lovesick heart, sorry, wait for me.

460
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:22,220
Panorama future,
the dazzling brightness will soon be here.

461
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:26,526
You understand, right?

462
00:25:26,576 --> 00:25:30,060
Sorry, wait for me.

